1. Product vision
Build a premium, modern, product-led ecommerce experience for electric commuter bikes. The experience should feel clean, confident, contemporary, trustworthy, and easy to shop.

The website must:
- Preserve the visual identity of the supplied reference image.
- Use the reference image and source Figma frames as the primary visual authority.
- Place the hero copy and calls to action on the left and the bicycle on the right on desktop.
- Show the bike in the correct real-world orientation. In the supplied reference, the front wheel and handlebars are on the left and the saddle/rear wheel are on the right. Never mirror a product asset if that makes its geometry, branding, drivetrain, motor, or other manufacturer details inaccurate.
- Use manufacturer-approved product names, color names, specs, and imagery wherever real product assets are supplied. Do not invent manufacturer facts.
- Make the website responsive, accessible, performant, and maintainable.
- Include subtle, polished motion, with a robust static/reduced-motion experience.
- Establish reusable tokens and components so all pages remain visually consistent.
- Complete a working implementation, not just a design proposal.
